# Supabase — Stage 1 (accounts and companies).
#
# Copy to `.env.local` for local development. On Vercel these are project
# environment variables and are already set.
#
# The app works with NONE of these set: sign-in is simply unavailable, and the
# editor, Save Project and Load Project behave exactly as they did before there
# was a backend. That is a supported state, not a broken one.
#
# Supabase is renaming its keys. The old pair (anon / service_role) and the new
# pair (publishable / secret) are BOTH read, new names first, so nothing breaks
# on the day the old ones are retired. Set whichever pair your project shows.

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT.supabase.co

# Browser-safe. It grants nothing on its own — row-level security is what makes
# it safe to ship to a client.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# SERVER ONLY. Bypasses row-level security entirely. Never prefix this with
# NEXT_PUBLIC_, and never import it into a client component. It is used in
# exactly two places, both of them before the person has an account: creating
# the auth user named by a valid invite, and deleting that user again if
# redeeming the invite then fails.
SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# Where password-reset and invite links point. Without it the app falls back to
# the request's own origin, which is right locally and wrong behind a proxy.
#
# ⚠ THIS IS THE CANONICAL HOST, and on 2026-10-18 it became strawpanels.com.
# Two separate things read it, and they fail differently:
#
#   - the password-reset link's `redirectTo`. Supabase REFUSES a redirect that
#     is not on the project's own allowlist, so this value and the allowlist in
#     Supabase > Authentication > URL Configuration have to agree or no reset
#     email works at all. (Since 2026-10-18 that refusal is reported instead of
#     being swallowed — see app/api/auth/password-reset/route.ts.)
#   - the company-invite link, which is only a string shown once in the UI.
#     A stale value here does not break it; it just points people at the old
#     host.
#
# ⚠ Pick ONE host and redirect the other to it at Vercel. The session cookie is
# host-only — `serverSession.ts` sets no `domain` — so strawpanels.com and
# www.strawpanels.com do NOT share a sign-in. Someone who signs in on one and
# lands on the other is simply signed out, with nothing on screen explaining
# why. The apex is canonical.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://strawpanels.com
